<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madhavrao I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1745">1745</a>–<a href="/years/1772">1772</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Madhavrao Peshwa, Madhav Rao I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madhavrao I (1745–1772) was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> from 1761 to 1772. Coming to office soon after the disaster of Panipat, he restored Maratha power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> and the north, defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizam of Hyderabad</a> and led repeated campaigns against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a>, forcing him to cede territory and pay tribute. His early death from tuberculosis at the age of twenty-seven weakened the Peshwa's government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/madhavrao-i.jpg" alt="Madhavrao I" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bhoj Raj · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madhavrao_I_Peshwa.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
